    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build. \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Rewrote the `customerCode` generation from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence, one more than the number of owners already in that city (counted via `findAll()` filtered by city, case-insensitively \u2014 consistent with the existing `AssignNamesakeCount` pattern), running before `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't counted.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 No code change needed. The `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) is built by concatenating `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`), as the spec requires for \"every value derived from the customerCode.\"\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` field descriptions and examples to document the new format.\n\n## Tests\n- The new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` \u2014 passes.\n- Full `mvn test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 run, 0 failures, 0 errors.",
